   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Validation rules applied at commit (the fold; each has exactly one named refusal):",
   "fontSize": 17,
   "fontFamily": 5,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "baseline": 15,
   "containerId": null,
   "originalText": "Validation rules applied at commit (the fold; each has exactly one named refusal):",
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "dc81ceda8bbb",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 60,
   "y": 496,
   "width": 946.12,
   "height": 105.0,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 1,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 420514790,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 217275225,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": null,
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "R1   weight \u2208 {0, 1, 2} \u2014 anything else is unrepresentable.\nR2   JOIN inserts at weight 0 only.          R3  LEAVE only at weight 0.\nR13  DOUBLE / HALVE are solitary batches.    R14 any other batch moves \u2264 1 unit of per-node mass (\u03a3|\u0394W| \u2264 1).\nR14 is over PER-NODE MASS, not net change: the one-era identity swap has net 0 but mass 2 and is refused.\nEra-safety invariant: every consecutive pair of configurations has intersecting majority families,\nso EVERY intermediate era is quorum-safe on its own \u2014 a leader dying mid-sequence leaves only safe eras.",
   "fontSize": 14,
   "fontFamily": 5,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "baseline": 12,
   "containerId": null,
   "originalText": "R1   weight \u2208 {0, 1, 2} \u2014 anything else is unrepresentable.\nR2   JOIN inserts at weight 0 only.          R3  LEAVE only at weight 0.\nR13  DOUBLE / HALVE are solitary batches.    R14 any other batch moves \u2264 1 unit of per-node mass (\u03a3|\u0394W| \u2264 1).\nR14 is over PER-NODE MASS, not net change: the one-era identity swap has net 0 but mass 2 and is refused.\nEra-safety invariant: every consecutive pair of configurations has intersecting majority families,\nso EVERY intermediate era is quorum-safe on its own \u2014 a leader dying mid-sequence leaves only safe eras.",
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "ffd0a6f2f7b8",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 60,
   "y": 700,
   "width": 864.28,
   "height": 21.25,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
